counterfactuals.output:
A vacuum transport assembly for a printing press, comprising:

a plurality of vacuum transport modules, each vacuum transport module having at least one inlet opening through which air is drawn to retain and transport a sheet or web of printing material;

wherein the vacuum transport modules are arranged adjacent one another in a direction transverse to a transport direction of the printing material;

wherein a combined transverse extent of the inlet openings is at least 80% of a working width of the printing press;

wherein each vacuum transport module is independently removable from the assembly without removal of the other vacuum transport modules; and

wherein each vacuum transport module is fluidically connectable to a vacuum source, the vacuum transport modules optionally being connected to a common suction line.
